00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:01.429 align:start position:0%
 
okay  last thing on again every day we are  learning more about the insanity that  took place in the aftermath of the  november election and the in the lead-up  to the january 6 riots by now  you have no doubt heard if you've been  watching my show listening to the  podcast over the last year  all of the different ways in which they  were trying to get a hold of the fact  that joe biden won the election and that  they wanted to try to overturn it we've  talked about  uh 63 court filings all of which were  found to be without merit some to be  some were found where there was no  standing and many of them found to be  without merit we've learned about oh  mike pence is going to flip the election  somehow  either by something he does himself or  by sending it back to the states or you  know whatever the case may be  we also heard about declaring a national  emergency slash martial law  and there was this idea of seizing the  voting machines now what you do with the  voting machines once you seize them to  flip results  we can speculate we don't exactly know  but we now have reason to believe that  donald trump himself  who's shocked by this donald trump  himself was much more involved than  previously known in the plan to seize  those voting machines the new york times  breaking the story this week  trump had role  in weighing proposals to seize voting  machines  new accounts show that the former  president was more directly involved  than previously known in plans developed  by outside advisors to use national  security agencies to seek evidence of  fraud  six weeks after election day with his  hold on power slipping trump directed  giuliani to make a remarkable call trump  wanted him to ask dhs  if it could legally take control of  voting machines in key swing states  three people familiar with the matter  said remember that giuliani did so  calling the department's acting deputy  secretary who said he lacked the  authority to audit or impound the  machines  trump pressed giuliani to make the  inquiry after rejecting a separate  effort by his outside advisors to have  the pentagon take control of the  machines and the outreach to the  department of homeland security came not  long after trump in an oval office  meeting with then attorney general  william barr  raised the possibility of whether the  justice department could seize the  machines a previously undisclosed  suggestion  that mr barr immediately shot down  the new accounts show that trump was  more directly involved than previously  known in exploring these proposals to  seize voting machines as he grasped  unsuccessfully for evidence of fraud  that could help him reverse the 2020  election  right now  everyone's attention  is focused on the coup  and on election fraud and that makes  sense but look at how much we've learned  just about that and then think imagine  for a moment  how much other  um  crazy stuff was going on that we still  don't know anything about that will  likely be uncovered about the last four  years  it will probably take  conservatively another four years  to figure all of that out and it could  even take closer to eight to ten years  for it all to shake out in terms of its  repercussions  um it's very clear that they did attempt  a coup  but they seemed not that competent at it  they seemed as competent at  doing the coup  as they were at governing when donald  trump was president and it failed and it  became a sideshow but we can't write it  off and not worry  because as i said earlier desantis is a  more competent trump and that makes him  more dangerous  and these same techniques now with the  experience of 2020 knowing where the  holdups were knowing where it ended up  stalling  with a more competent person at the helm  could be a very dangerous proposition  and we've heard from  retired military generals who say if  trump had had the generals on his side  could have been a very different outcome  we've heard about um if there had been  more willingness in the house and  particularly the senate  to  uh attempt to reject or challenge some  of the results in a more serious way in  multiple states  it could have been a different outcome  now one more thought about this uh trump  role  in trying to seize voting machines  remember when william barr quit  seemingly out of the blue as attorney  general on december 23rd december 23rd  was the date of william barr's  resignation letter  did william barr  see the writing on the wall about what  was coming on january 6th maybe not  specifically but knowing this is  potentially bad and i don't want to be  associated with it and that's why he  abruptly quit because if you consider  the timing the meetings where the idea  of a national emergency was floated  the meetings where the question about  can we seize the voting machines all of  this stuff happened between the november  election  and december 23rd when william barr quit  and it seems plausible at least that  barr knew or suspected that something  insane was coming and decided to get the  hell out of there before it did doesn't  make barr any better of an attorney  general  it's just bar acting out of  self-interest the timing makes sense at  some point maybe we'll know for sure

